/* v4.6.395: YOUR BODY, LATELY. The last-7-days grid becomes a body map: front and back,
   each muscle tinted by how many days since it last had work -- brightest today, a step
   fainter each day, gone at six. Tap a body part to see what its exercises lean on.

   Two readings, kept apart on purpose:
     RECENCY  (the card)        -- colour means DAYS SINCE, nothing else. A muscle counts as
                                   worked on a day when it gets one set as the main muscle,
                                   or two sets as a helper.
     EMPHASIS (an exercise)     -- colour means how much that one exercise leans on each
                                   muscle: the main muscle full, helpers lighter, the chest
                                   graded top-to-bottom for incline and decline work.
   Neither is a measurement. Emphasis is a rough illustration from the exercise's usual
   form ("varies with technique" says so on screen); it is not activation, recovery or
   readiness, and the copy does not claim to be.

   Where the numbers come from: the main muscle is exMuscle() (js/derive.js) -- the same
   table every other card reads, your own setting for an exercise you made, the part's
   default otherwise. Helpers come from BM_HELP below. An exercise with neither (a custom
   Legs movement with no muscle set) lights the whole part faintly rather than guessing
   one muscle. Regions come from js/bodymap-data.js, generated from the approved artwork
   by tools/bodymap/build.py. */

